{
  "_help": [
    "Keyword rules for comment sentiment. Edit freely, then run `npm run retag-comments` to re-tag stored comments.",
    "Matching ignores case and works on whole words or phrases, so 'issue' does not match inside 'tissue'. End a keyword with * to match any word starting with it: 'complain*' matches complain, complaint, complaints.",
    "Rules are checked in the order listed: the first sentiment that matches wins. Negative comes first so a real complaint is never hidden as Spam or Careers.",
    "unless: if any of these words or phrases is in the comment, the rule is skipped ('great job' is praise, not a job seeker; an owner asking about servicing is a question, not a lead).",
    "links_except: any link to a site not in this list makes the comment match (used for Spam; subdomains count, so dealers.montraelectric.com is allowed).",
    "question_mark: true also counts any comment containing '?' as that sentiment.",
    "Comments that match nothing get the fallback sentiment.",
    "needs_response lists the sentiments that get the 'Needs response' flag. Careers and Spam are never flagged, and neither are comments written by the Montra page itself.",
    "X mentions use the same rules, with links and leading @handles removed first. Media and brand-page tweets are labelled 'Media mention' and flagged only when Negative (see lib/x.ts)."
  ],
